[wistron][ztp] preserve VLAN Option 67 across DHCP handoff

SONiC publishes DHCP ZTP data through one global URL and owner lock. With
eth0, front-panel and the Wistron VLAN DHCP client running concurrently, a
VLAN BOUND can lose the lock race. A later STOP/RELEASE from the old owner
then removes the only URL while the VLAN keeps its valid lease, leaving
ztp-engine in discovery without another BOUND event.

Keep an atomic per-interface DHCP candidate set under a flock. Prefer a
valid Vlan candidate, and promote another candidate when the current owner
exits. Accept TIMEOUT only while its leased address remains configured.

Install a VLAN DHCP server route hook so an off-subnet DHCP server
identifier is reached through the router learned on that VLAN before the
Option 67 URL becomes visible. Store route data with each candidate so a
promoted owner restores the matching route. Start the custom VLAN dhclient
as a single owned instance with canonical per-interface PID and lease
files, and serialize its lifecycle with a separate control lock.

Close the lifecycle lock descriptor before launching dhclient. Otherwise
the background daemon inherits fd 8 and holds the flock for its lifetime,
causing later install/remove operations to time out.

Enable this opt-in VLAN workaround for Wistron ES1227 36TS/54TS HWSKUs.
During teardown, stop only the exact PID/start-time pair created by this
workaround and clear discovery state after all DHCP exit hooks finish.

Verification:
- dash/bash syntax checks for all changed hooks and scripts
- Ethernet11 BOUND, Vlan951 BOUND, Ethernet11 RELEASE retains the URL
  with dhcp:Vlan951 as owner
- 200 concurrent Vlan951 BOUND / Ethernet11 RELEASE handoffs
- Vlan951 RELEASE removes the final URL, owner and candidate route
- fake-ip route-hook checks for BOUND, TIMEOUT and terminal cleanup
- launched DHCP child does not inherit lifecycle-lock fd 8

